# {{ org_name }} engineering knowledge

Shared engineering knowledge for {{ org_name }}: postmortems, shared runbooks and the incident
taxonomy. Everything is Markdown with YAML frontmatter in Git, so agents and people read and write
it the same way, and every change goes through a pull request.

Service-specific knowledge stays in each service repo: approved ADRs and runbooks in `docs/`,
generated wiki pages in `kuan-workbench/wiki/`.

## Layout

| Path | Content |
|---|---|
| `postmortems/<year>/<id>-<slug>.md` | Incident postmortems, one file per incident |
| `runbooks-shared/` | Runbooks that apply to more than one service |
| `taxonomy.md` | The standard incident categories |
| `templates/postmortem.md` | Template for a new postmortem |
| `templates/adr.md` | Template for an ADR (ADRs live in the service repo under `docs/adr/`) |
| `scripts/check-frontmatter.py` | Validates postmortem frontmatter (run in CI) |
| `scripts/build-index.py` | Builds the level-1 JSON index of postmortems and runbooks |
| `scripts/stale-wiki-check.sh` | Reports stale generated wiki pages in a service repo |

## Scripts

All scripts need Python 3.11+ with PyYAML (`pip install pyyaml`).

```sh
python3 scripts/check-frontmatter.py            # exit 0 valid, 1 problems, 2 taxonomy missing
python3 scripts/build-index.py --out index.json # JSON index; regenerate any time
scripts/stale-wiki-check.sh ../order-service    # STALE / UNKNOWN lines; exit 1 if any
```

CI (`.github/workflows/knowledge-ci.yml`) runs the frontmatter check and builds the index on every
push and pull request.

## Rules

- Postmortems are blameless: describe systems and processes, not individuals.
- Remove personal data before committing.
- Use a category from `taxonomy.md`. Shared categories are what make repeat incidents countable.
- Postmortems and ADRs are immutable once approved; update action items, or supersede an ADR with
  a new one.

